Subject: [PATCH 2/6] refactor(daemon): R8a step 4 the antigravity permission
 grant takes fileLock and writer from the host runtime

Folded into step 5 as the R8a report recommended: the executor's runtime now exists, so the launcher passes runtime.fileLock /
runtime.writer into resolveMcpBridgeForRun. The ports test (lock, backup, write, unlock order; failing backup / write / lock three
ways) was red first (7 failures) and is green; an executor-level pin shows the grant going through the host runtime. The attempt
patch from the R8a report was applied minus its platform defaults.

